{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 10, 15]], "date-time": "2026-10-15T19:40:33Z", "timestamp": 1792093233284, "version": "4.4.0"}, "reference-count": 269, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "50", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2023, 2, 22]], "date-time": "2023-02-22T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1677024000000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/termsAndConditions#vor"}], "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/501100001809", "name": "National Natural Science Foundation of China", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["51788104"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["51788104"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100001809", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/501100001809", "name": "National Natural Science Foundation of China", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["U21A2080"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["U21A2080"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100001809", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["Advanced Materials"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2023, 12]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title><jats:p>Solid\u2010state batteries (SSBs) are considered as one of the most promising candidates for the next\u2010generation energy\u2010storage technology, because they simultaneously exhibit high safety, high energy density, and wide operating temperature range. The replacement of liquid electrolytes with solid electrolytes produces numerous solid\u2013solid interfaces within the SSBs. A thorough understanding on the roles of these interfaces is indispensable for the rational performance optimization. In this review, the interface issues in the SSBs, including internal buried interfaces within solid electrolytes and composite electrodes, and planar interfaces between electrodes and solid electrolyte separators or current collectors are discussed. T